✔ remove preserves other bases, nested ':' bases and unrelated caches, and reports a failed worker unregister (9.1118ms)
✔ two pages sharing one cache cannot prepare different versions or remove during a prepare; the pointer always names a complete retained cache (16.7066ms)
✔ without Web Locks the offline copy is refused rather than mutated unprotected (6.224ms)
✔ unsupported contexts and server failures are explicit (0.619ms)
✔ service worker serves only the adopted manifest set inside its own scope and never mixes the network in (11.4658ms)
✔ a tampered or unreadable adopted set is refused, never executed and never mixed with the network (13.2197ms)
✔ a warm worker re-validates the stored manifest on every request instead of trusting a memoized copy (8.7345ms)
✔ the service worker build is part of the shell version, so a worker-only update is never silently complete (22.9909ms)
✔ a failed pointer write during a worker-changing update leaves the previous worker and adopted shell runnable offline (16.9352ms)
✔ a failed worker registration restores the previous adoption record (15.8729ms)
